Phasmid: media devices

What:     enumerateDevices() lists the profile's devices, never the host's,
          after the virtual entries the claimed OS puts first in each audio
          kind ("Default" on Linux; "Default - ..." and "Communications -
          ..." on Windows). Blanking before permission and the per-origin
          hash stay stock; the ID salt derives from the seed per storage key.
          Host hot-plugs fire no devicechange. Capture on a claimed device
          rejects with NotReadableError; "default" input opens the host's
          microphone.
Why:      Headless and Xvfb have no capture devices while a desktop has real
          ones, and the host's labels and counts identify it.
Profile:  media_devices.audioinput, media_devices.audiooutput,
          media_devices.videoinput, media_devices.labels.*, seed, os.family
Hooks:    content/browser/renderer_host/media/media_devices_manager.cc
          MediaDevicesManager::DevicesEnumerated, new GetProfileDevices;
          content/browser/media/media_devices_util.cc
          GetMediaDeviceSaltAndOrigin, GotSalt
Contexts: main, iframe, before and after permission; workers have no
          navigator.mediaDevices
Guard:    tests/guards/platform/media-devices.py

